I can't tell from your post if you're already doing this or not, but
generally whenever you have to fight a group of several monsters --
whether they be ants or bees or orcs -- the best way to do it is to
face them one at a time in a tunnel or a doorway.  That way only one
of the monsters can hit you at a time, and you have a clear way out if
you need to run.

Also, whenever your hit points start dropping, running is a good idea.
Being burdened slows you down, so you generally shouln't do that; if
you ever do need to carry that much stuff, try to avoid fighting and
immediately drop the excess baggage if you do end up in a fight.  Also
remember that monsters can't follow you to another level (except for
pets and a few high-level monsters if they're standing right next to
you) and most (like ants) can't open doors or move boulders.

If you, for some reason, can't run away, a scroll of teleport can be a
very useful get-out-trouble card.  Conversely, a wand of teleport can
make the trouble itself go away, at least for a while.  Note that if
you somehow end up in a situation where you're surrounded by monsters
on all sides, as a last resort you can break the wand (by (a)pplying
it) to teleport all the monsters next to you.

Arrows, daggers and other missile weapons are also a good way to kill
enemies from a distance, before they can get close enough to hurt you.
It's a good idea to practice fighting with them and to #enhance your
skill with them as soon as possible, since higher skill levels not
only improve your accuracy but let you fire multiple missiles at once
(as long as you have a large enough stack).  You should normally pick
one class of missile weapons and concentrate on that; for many classes
daggers will be the best choice, but some will do better with arrows.
Other possibilities are darts, knives and rocks (with a sling), but
few people seem to recommend specializing in them.

